TASK: TDD collision resolution (Phase 4)

ACCEPTANCE
- Hitboxes derived from map data: houses become boxes at their lot centres sized
  by the same HOUSE_LOT_FIT (0.86) cap the renderer scales their models to, and
  props reuse TownGrid's published collision radii. Ids come from the grid, so a
  bonk is traceable to the house or prop it happened to.
- Swept, not sampled: one frame at 1.6 u/s covers enough ground to pass clean
  through a prop, so contact is found along the motion segment. The sweep stops
  a CONTACT_SKIN (1mm) short so the next frame does not start in contact.
- Circle-vs-circle is solved exactly (quadratic); circle-vs-box is a slab test
  against the radius-inflated box, which squares the corners and can stop the
  car up to ~0.1*radius early on a diagonal — erring early, so the car is never
  seen inside a wall.
- Crashable props are bumped once per route and then driven past; buildings
  consume the leg that ran into them. The route cursor only ever advances, so a
  stuck state is impossible by construction.
- The body flattens to 25% and spreads to 15% over the recoil, read from the
  motor's bounce progress, so the animation cannot disagree with the motion.

TWO REAL DEFECTS FOUND BY VERIFYING IN THE BROWSER (both now pinned by tests)
1. Recoil direction. The bounce originally reversed the car's heading. A car
   that stopped fractionally inside the inflated box (a square corner) bounced
   exactly the wrong way — into the wall — and repeating the tap walked it
   further in each time. Live, 12 bonks in 1.4s ended with the car standing
   inside a house's hitbox. The recoil now comes from the contact geometry, and
   a car found overlapping is pushed out along the surface's shortest exit.
   Re-verified live: 28 mashed re-targets of the same house, no penetration.
2. Test expectations, twice: an arrival asserted within 5mm when the motor
   stops at ARRIVAL_RADIUS (0.25), and a start position that turned out to be
   already overlapping a house's corner.

COVERAGE
- collision.ts, vehicleMotor.ts, vehicleActor.ts: 100% statements, branches,
  functions and lines. 229 tests across 18 files; biome clean, tsc clean.
- Also removed as unreachable rather than covered: a `?? 0` on a variable the
  caller guarantees, a division the sweep's pull-back makes unnecessary, and a
  ternary arm proven dead by the guard above it.

DEFERRED (with a reason, not silently)
- Bonk audio is the AudioEngine's (Phase 5): FR8 requires first-tap unlock, a
  kid-safe master gain cap and a mute node around every sound, so a bare blip
  now would be thrown away. The event is available as motor.bonkCount().
